## 4. Current Product Health (NPS, 2025)

This is the honest picture — not the sales pitch.

- **Portal NPS: +32** (292 responses) — reasonable baseline; users can complete core tasks
- **Booking & Payments NPS: -1** (174 responses) — near-even split between promoters and detractors

### Key pain areas (by priority)

1. **Booking Workflow** *(23 mentions — Critical)*
   Users cannot edit bookings after creation, cannot add time mid-session, no drag-and-drop, and customers cannot self-serve. The day/time overview is considered unclear and requires too many clicks.

2. **Payments & Integrations** *(20 mentions — Critical)*
   No split payment (cash + card), no saved cards, limited payment provider flexibility, POS integration gaps, missing international payment support (particularly Africa).

3. **Memberships** *(19 mentions — High, highest emotional intensity)*
   Perks are tied to calendar month rather than billing cycle — a well-known pain point with real business impact. Membership creation is complex, editing is cumbersome, and customers cannot self-manage.

4. **Reporting & Data Export** *(13 mentions — High)*
   No easy CSV/Excel export, inflexible filtering, visit tracking and usage hours not surfaced, payment reconciliation is insufficient.

5. **Mobile / Responsive Design** *(12 mentions — High)*
   Portal does not adapt well to mobile. No dedicated app. Mobile Safari usage confirmed in device data but experience is not optimised.

> **Note:** Tournaments & Leagues feedback is handled by a separate team and excluded from these findings.

