## 5. Technical Context

### Codebase
- YGB was built from scratch by Jake (the original founder), who recently rolled off the project. His deep knowledge of the codebase was a bottleneck for developers, and that knowledge transfer is still in progress.
- The codebase is complex and has been heavily customised for specific edge cases over time. This makes it difficult to remove functionality without risk — changes need careful consideration.
- Junior developers cannot be hired for this reason. The team needs engineers who can navigate a non-trivial, legacy-adjacent system.

### Design system
- YGB has its **own design system**, separate from Trackman's.
- The current **Trackman Design System is not compatible** with the YGB design system.
- A **new Trackman Design System is in development** — migration to it is planned but cannot begin until it is released. Until then, we work within the existing YGB system.
- The migration will eventually bring B&P in line with the broader Trackman product family visually and technically.

### Integration model
- B&P is embedded in the Trackman Portal as an **iFrame**.
- Trackman and YGB/B&P maintain **separate data models** synced via APIs — not a single shared database.
- Trackman hardware (bays, simulators) is linked to B&P entities (venues, bays) through API matching.

